-- issue #1191: a top-level binding whose name collides with a prelude STANDALONE
-- (not an interface method -- stdlib/core.mdk's `export sum : (Foldable t, Num a)
-- => t a -> a`) is not shadowed on the zero-non-core-import single-file `check`
-- path. The user's own declared signature (`Int -> Int -> Int`) is discarded and
-- the body is typechecked against the PRELUDE's scheme instead, producing
-- `Cannot construct infinite type involving a` -- citing the prelude's OWN type
-- variable, not anything the user wrote. This is standalone-vs-standalone, which
-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS S1 (docs/spec/SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md) does not cover: S1 is
-- defined only over funDef-names ∩ iface-method-names.
sum : Int -> Int -> Int
sum a b = a + b

main = println (sum 1 2)
